* BORDER CONFIG -- VM/370plus 9.12c/d: BORDER, the LAN's way out.
* BORDER (10.1.4.2 on the CTC pair 0606/0607) passes a connection from
* the PC to one of its ports on to a guest on the LAN:
*   EXPOSE protocol port TO address [port]
* protocol is TCP or UDP; the second port defaults to the first.
* Everything else from outside is dropped; ssh to BORDER itself (22)
* stays open.  BORDER also gives guests without an address of their
* own one by DHCP (10.3.0.100-199) and passes name lookups to the
* name server below (default: the PC, 10.1.4.1):
*   DNS address
* Restart BORDER after a change (FORCE BORDER, then
* AUTOLOG BORDER BORDER).
EXPOSE TCP 2222 TO 10.3.0.2 22
EXPOSE TCP 2223 TO 10.3.0.3 22
